//! The `margin-trim` property allows the container to trim the margins of its children where they
//! adjoin the container's edges.
//!
//! Initial: none. Inherited: no.
//! Percentages: not accepted.
//!
//! Keyword effects:
//! - block: Margins provided to the block children where they adjoin the container's edges are
//! trimmed to zero without affecting the margins provided to the container.
//! - block-end: Margin of last block child with the container's edge is trimmed to zero.
//! - block-start: Margin of the first block child with the container's edge is trimmed to zero.
//! - none: Margins are not trimmed by the container.
//!
//! Grammar: none | block | [ block-start || block-end ]
//!
//! Specification: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-box-4/#propdef-margin-trim
//!
//! Author guide: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/margin-trim
//!
//! Purpose and value descriptions adapted from MDN contributors (CC-BY-SA-2.5).
//!
//! Generated from @webref/css 8.7.8. Do not edit.

